Format specifiers: used for storing the value, interaction between the user and source code.
eg: 
int  - %d, %o-octal, %x-hexa, %i-integer
char
- These both are integral
float - approximate value
double - estimated value
- These both are real/floating point

- There is no format specifier for binary(0 / 1)
